Policy plus helpers for crash-safe writes.  Crash safety in this
system is layered: the loader writes caches atomically (tmp+rename in
~cyberdeck-emacs--cache-write~) and readers validate with rescan
fallback, so a killed boot self-heals.  This file gives cyberdeck code the
same primitive and a verification command.  Nothing here runs at load;
all helpers are runtime-only, so load order is irrelevant.

** Atomic write helper
#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun my/cyberdeck-atomic-write (path insert-fn)
  "Write PATH atomically: INSERT-FN runs in a temp buffer, then rename.
INSERT-FN takes no arguments and inserts the full file content.
Never leaves a half-written file behind.  Signals on failure."
  (let ((tmp (concat path ".tmp")))
    (make-directory (file-name-directory path) t)
    (with-temp-file tmp
      (funcall insert-fn))
    (rename-file tmp path t)))
#+end_src

** Verify persistence health
#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun my/cyberdeck-verify-persistence ()
  "Check index, eval cache, and known-keys record for readability.
Returns (LABEL . OK) rows; interactive shows a summary.  Read-only:
repairs are explicit (delete the corrupt file and reload to rebuild)."
  (interactive)
  (let* ((home (expand-file-name "~"))
         (idx (expand-file-name ".config/emacs/.local/cache/discovery-index.el" home))
         (rows nil))
    (push (cons "discovery-index"
                (condition-case nil
                    (progn (with-temp-buffer
                             (insert-file-contents idx)
                             (read (current-buffer)))
                           t)
                  (error nil)))
          rows)
    (push (cons "known-keys"
                (let ((p (and (fboundp 'my/cyberdeck-links--known-keys-path)
                              (my/cyberdeck-links--known-keys-path))))
                  (and p (file-exists-p p))))
          rows)
    (when (called-interactively-p 'any)
      (message "persistence: %s"
               (mapconcat (lambda (r) (format "%s=%s" (car r) (if (cdr r) "ok" "BAD")))
                          (nreverse rows) " ")))
    rows))
#+end_src
